The separation metrics of dimensionality-reduction evaluation count each group once: one weight per sample, in the scaling, the fit and the balanced accuracy, gives each class the same weight and, within a class, each group the same, so a subject with many epochs no longer outweighs the others and a subject with samples in both classes counts once in each. With one sample per group the logistic-regression score is unchanged. The random forest uses 200 trees instead of 300, 1.5 times faster with the same scores within its seed-to-seed spread.
